  <section|Exact mathematical scope><label|exact-mathematical-scope>

  The outer radius is (B=\\operatorname{radiusB}(x)=\\lceil(\\log
  x)^2\\rceil). The reader panel radius is the source's
  <strong|natural-number quotient>

  <\equation*>
    p=<math-up|boxCharge><around|(|x|)>=<around*|\<lfloor\>|<around|(|B+80|)>/20|\<rfloor\>>,
  </equation*>

  not the real quotient. The article proves the geometric inequalities for
  (B\\ge200):

  <\equation*>
    30*p\<less\>11*B+1-p,<space|1em>9*p\<leqslant\>B,<space|1em>B/4+p+B/50\<leqslant\>B/2,<space|1em>B/4+2*p+B/25\<leqslant\>B,<space|1em>p+B/50+B/4+B/2\<leqslant\>B.
  </equation*>

  Here <verbatim|Clears> at outer B excludes the seed dome of radius
  <verbatim|10B+B+1>. <verbatim|Translate> supplies an onto bijection of
  actual and cleared panel labels, using <verbatim|clearance> to prove
  range/liveness. It does <strong|not> equate the curved and identity row
  Gram entries. Instead the manuscript derives the source change from the
  rowwise frozen cancellation, chart estimates, and a cutoff-plus-tail
  estimate; derives the actual mean via the normal residual identity and its
  local inverse/tail split; and derives the inverse-column bound by an
  entrywise Gram perturbation followed by the finite resolvent identity. The
  two distinct positive Gram gaps are retained.

  The stated outputs are the actual mean error (x^{-7/8}) and the
  actual-to-cleared panel inverse-column error (x^{-1/4}), for a fixed
  payment multiplier R and source parameter
  0\<less\>=t\<less\>=R*clearanceFare(x), with coarse period
  c\<gtr\>=100(1+B), the stored-flag equality, and the same pose/history
  across all queried centers. The mean coordinate is active and within B/4 of
  the target; the inverse-column indices lie in its panel. The exact
  outer-scale price, clearance and path receipts. The later cut-head split to
  the full physical covariance is expressly excluded from the theorem.

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Fully qualified source
  declaration>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned path and checked mathematical
  role>>>|<row|<cell|Exact panel radius>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.boxCharge>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.stockBound>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/ChipHeal.lean>.
  The first is natural division <verbatim|(radiusB x + 80)/20>; the second
  proves every sector address lies within that radius.>>|<row|<cell|Outer
  radius and path cutoff>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Pressure.radiusB>,
  <verbatim|YM.Pressure.Stores.till>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Pressure/Seeds.lean>.
  Here <verbatim|radiusB x=ceil((log x)^2)> and <verbatim|till x=radiusB
  x/100000>. The former supplies the explicit stretched-log tail estimate;
  the latter truncates paths, not the direction.>>|<row|<cell|Two-scale
  clearance arithmetic>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.Clears>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.live_test>>|<cell|<verbatim|ChipHeal.lean>.
  Clearance excludes the halo with radius <verbatim|10*radiusB x + D + 1>; at
  <verbatim|D=B> this is <verbatim|11B+1>. The live test uses this dome
  exclusion and triangle inequality.>>|<row|<cell|Fixed-row base
  difference>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.base_summary>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/Staged.lean>.
  Its output is <verbatim|\|Rows.base - firstTerm\| \<less\>= C*t*widen (till
  x) t tau>. The proof obtains the upper/lower chart and kernel-chart costs,
  applies the product-difference split for <verbatim|zip>, and preserves the
  same <verbatim|V,v> and row.>>|<row|<cell|Nonlinear pulse versus uncut
  ideal>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.prepared>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.pulse_cost>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.ideal_tail>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.peon>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/Watch.lean>.
  The direction is cut at the outer comparison radius D=B by finite row
  dependence. Separately, the path sum is cut at <verbatim|till x=B/100000>;
  the finite pulse cost is <verbatim|A*(1+till x)*t*\|\|a\|\|>, while the
  weighted omitted-path tail is <verbatim|C*\|\|a\|\|*exp(-sigma*till x)>.
  This distinction is used in the manuscript.>>|<row|<cell|Response-size
  bound>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.carry_summary>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/TurnZero.lean>.
  Gives the bound on the frozen response norm by a constant times the
  direction norm.>>|<row|<cell|Frozen row
  cancellation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.rowzero>>|<cell|<verbatim|TurnZero.lean>.
  Exact pointwise identity <verbatim|Flat.ideal T (doc T F v) + firstTerm T v
  = 0>. This is substituted before estimating the kept-row
  difference.>>|<row|<cell|Source error after
  cancellation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.accounting>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/Subtotal.lean>.
  The selected credit is the row normalization times
  <verbatim|(base-firstTerm)+(marked bump-flat ideal)>. <verbatim|rowzero>
  cancels <verbatim|firstTerm+flat ideal> before absolute values.
  <verbatim|base_summary> supplies the first difference, and
  <verbatim|prepared> restricts the direction at outer radius B while
  truncating paths at <verbatim|till x>, using its finite pulse cost and
  weighted omitted-path tail; <verbatim|carry_summary> supplies the
  frozen-response norm. Their combination proves <verbatim|\|credit\|
  \<less\>= A*t*widen (till x) t tau> on receipt rows within B/2. The fixed
  data include one patch/tube/configuration/frozen forest/pose, outer
  clearance, flags, paid local price, and
  <verbatim|AgreeNear>.>>|<row|<cell|Normal residual and local
  solve>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.spacing>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.focused>>|<cell|<verbatim|Subtotal.lean>.
  The hypotheses require the coarse side <verbatim|c.val\<gtr\>=100*(1+radiusB
  x)>, the target within B/4 and the source flags equal to the posed
  configuration flags. <verbatim|spacing> proves <verbatim|offCenter(pane W Q
  0)y-x=(Q*pane-I)^T x-pane^T(Qx+y)>. <verbatim|focused> substitutes the
  exact row Gram identity <verbatim|Q a+b=M^T(Ma+f')>, bounds the residual by
  summing at most <verbatim|D=pieces P G * LocalJet.grain (span P x)> source
  rows, and uses the local inverse row/column sums plus the
  central-coordinate exponential inverse-window tail. No global operator-norm
  bound for the padded-window error is asserted.>>|<row|<cell|Canonical mean
  normal identities>|<cell|equations <verbatim|eq:mean-error-identity>,
  <verbatim|eq:mean-point>, <verbatim|eq:mean-remote-final>>|<cell|Parent
  <verbatim|/private/tmp/ym-existence-20261111/manuscript/existence/local-mean.tex>,
  section <verbatim|sec:local-mean>, SHA256
  <verbatim|f32876889ca48172b9399bafc1ff983ae0eee0750d4d7dd4329c2211ce60f1b5>.
  Reused for its exact (m-v=E^<em|v-P^>(Av+\\ell)) algebra and fixed-window
  bound; the present article does not substitute p for the outer B in the
  source matrices/cutoff.>>|<row|<cell|Mean
  payment>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.mean_shot>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.pay_mean>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Lift.plume>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/Cues.lean>.
  <verbatim|pay_mean> proves the displayed allowance after setting
  (t=R,\\text{clearanceFare}(x)). The actual price is
  <verbatim|16*(2*(radiusB x+1)+1)^5*card PlaqAxes*temp x>;
  <verbatim|temp_cost> at (1/32), <verbatim|plume>, the polynomial
  prefactors, and the exponential tails yield (x^{-7/8}).
  <verbatim|mean_shot> turns this estimate into the actual local mean
  statement with the same agreement and paid pose.>>|<row|<cell|Per-entry row
  perturbation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.stamps>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.local_gram>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/Movers.lean>.
  With <verbatim|wiggle=A*(1+till x)*t>, <verbatim|stamps> gives
  actual-vs-identity row error at most wiggle and identity row size at most
  A. <verbatim|local_gram> splits products as
  <verbatim|a_i(a_j-b_j)+(a_i-b_i)b_j> and sums at most <verbatim|pieces *
  LocalJet.grain(span)> contributing rows, producing <verbatim|matter =
  D*((A+wiggle)*wiggle+wiggle*A)>. Thus Gram entries are controlled, not
  identified.>>|<row|<cell|Finite inverse
  comparison>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.switches>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.chip_repair>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/ChipHeal.lean>.
  <verbatim|switches> is the ordinary identity
  (X^{-1}-Y^{-1}=X^{-1}(Y-X)Y^{-1}) on matched principal panels, with the
  square of the panel-count bound and both spectral gaps.
  <verbatim|chip_repair> packages this as <verbatim|clockChip> and uses
  <verbatim|Translate> only to reindex.>>|<row|<cell|Cleared panel
  bijection>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.staff_W>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.Translate>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.clearance>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.staff_inj>>|<cell|<verbatim|ChipHeal.lean>.
  <verbatim|staff_W> preserves membership; <verbatim|clearance> proves a bare
  panel address lies in the official-map range from outer clearance;
  injectivity plus this range proof makes <verbatim|Translate> onto. No
  entrywise Gram equality is used.>>|<row|<cell|Covariance
  charge/exponent>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.census>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.fares>,
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Remote.matter>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/NearDelay.lean>
  and <verbatim|Movers.lean>. <verbatim|census> is panel-count squared times
  both inverse-gap factors times the row perturbation. <verbatim|fares>
  bounds it by a polynomial (Z(x)\\le x^{1/8}) times temperature
  (\\vartheta(x)\\le x^{-1/2+1/8}), giving (x^{-1/4}). The fixed-multiplier
  transfer <verbatim|matter(A,Rt)\\le matter(RA,t)> is proved as
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.WeightedGaussianMarginal45C.Venue.alter> in
  <verbatim|Venue/Chips.lean>.>>|<row|<cell|Actual reader
  consumer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.WeightedGaussianMarginal45C.Venue.aperture>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.StrongScope.sight>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.scopes>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/WEIGHTED_GAUSSIAN_MARGINAL_LIMIT_45C/Venue/Chips.lean>
  and <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Focusing.lean>.
  <verbatim|aperture> relocates a target to an outer-clear pose and consumes
  mean plus chip-repair receipts, returning the (x^{-7/8}) mean and
  (x^{-1/4}) actual/bare panel covariance-column bounds. <verbatim|scopes>
  then applies its separate palette/covariance sandwich; this chapter does
  not claim that final split.>>|<row|<cell|Pose at shifted
  centers>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Pose.center>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Pose.lean>.
  It supplies clear, agreement and payment only for centers satisfying the
  original <verbatim|separation + walls \<less\>= W> margin. This precise
  margin is retained for every queried center.>>>>>

  <section|Other manuscript inputs reused><label|other-manuscript-inputs-reused>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Parent <verbatim|local-covariance.tex>, section
    <verbatim|sec:local-covariance>, SHA256
    <verbatim|29461555fd5eeb24f58f1a4d4ec2896fb4cb85ae60bc3c4aa03248ddc2e86218>:
    principal inverse floors, exponential inverse entries, and finite window
    tails.

    <item>Parent <verbatim|principal-comparison-jets.tex>, section
    <verbatim|sec:principal-comparison-jets>, SHA256
    <verbatim|ff624cbd11db727d32b9c3c50cf5540d2a048efb46e3e83b6c05c8b64dd1dded>:
    fixed-window identities; this output makes no new higher-jet claim.
  </itemize-minus>

  The subpower bounds use the imported source's <verbatim|till>,
  <verbatim|temp_cost(1/32)>, <verbatim|plume>, and scale estimates.
  <verbatim|R> is fixed before taking the large-x tail; the multiplier is
  absorbed by the proved monotonicity <verbatim|matter(A,Rt)\<less\>=matter(RA,t)>.
  The article records the elementary exponent arithmetic but does not prove
  the global growth law for B or manufacture the incoming path/gap budgets.

  <section|Commands and checks><label|commands-and-checks>

  Read-only commands run: targeted <verbatim|rg -n>/<verbatim|sed>
  inspections of the source files in the table; reads of the three parent
  canonical TeX chapters; pin read from <verbatim|source/upstream.json>;
  <verbatim|shasum -a 256> on the manuscript, evidence and canonical files;
  trailing-whitespace <verbatim|awk> scan (exit 0). <verbatim|python3
  scripts/check_blueprint.py> was attempted and returned exit 1 because this
  isolated clone lacks <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>; the
  bounded output contract allows only this TeX and evidence file, so no
  metadata was added. No Lean build or full manuscript build was run.
  Independent review is pending; this remains a draft.

